**task_01 — Fix #709: enforce `/read` and `/plan` mode on sub-agent tools** (product, `src/tool_wrappers.rs` + `src/tools.rs` + CLAUDE.md)
A broken safety promise, and the highest-value thing on the board. build_sub_agent_tool_at_depth gives children directory restrictions only — no mode guard — because with_read_guard* are Box<dyn AgentTool>-only and the sub-agent path is Arc. A child dispatched under /read can write freely. Fix: make ReadModeGuardTool hold an Arc, add *_arc constructors (existing Box entry points unchanged, zero call-site churn), apply them to the child's write-class tools and bash. Scope boundary stated explicitly: child bash still skips safety.rs outside modes — that half stays out, #709 stays open with an honest comment. Tests first, #[serial] (mode state is global), clippy run explicitly.

